1
00:00:05,413 --> 00:00:09,086
The Life Of Muhammadﷺ, The Makkan Period,

2
00:00:09,344 --> 00:00:10,998
by Imam Anwar Al-Alwlaki,

3
00:00:12,168 --> 00:00:14,857
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

4
00:00:14,939 --> 00:00:20,357
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

5
00:00:21,504 --> 00:00:28,996
An-Najashi(النجاشي), the Negus, refused to hand over the Muslims to the delegation of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

6
00:00:29,789 --> 00:00:34,916
And soon as both the Muslims, and the delegation of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) left.

7
00:00:35,325 --> 00:00:40,416
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) threatened that I'm going to make a comeback,

8
00:00:41,230 --> 00:00:43,385
وَاَسْتَعْسِلُوْخَزْرَاَهُمْ

9
00:00:43,672 --> 00:00:46,400
And I'm going to bring an end to the Muslims.

10
00:00:47,101 --> 00:00:52,351
Abdullah Bin Rabiyah(عبدالله بن ربيعة), or his partner let's say this partner, since there's a difference on the name,

11
00:00:52,955 --> 00:00:56,654
his partner said: No, don't do that, they are still our relatives.

12
00:00:56,802 --> 00:00:58,758
I mean, you don't have to go that far.

13
00:00:59,370 --> 00:01:02,837
Fine! He refused to hand them over let's just go back.

14
00:01:03,245 --> 00:01:05,767
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said: No, tomorrow I'm going to come back.

15
00:01:06,082 --> 00:01:10,387
And I'm going to tell the king that they say that Jesus is a slave.

16
00:01:12,310 --> 00:01:16,556
He did go the next day and he said they say, some bad things about Jesus,

17
00:01:16,609 --> 00:01:19,371
 they claim but he's a slave and he's not the Son of God.

18
00:01:20,271 --> 00:01:24,715
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) does not believe in all of this stuff anyway, but it's just to cause Fitnah(فتنه).

19
00:01:26,252 --> 00:01:29,085
So, An-Najashi(النجاشي) obviously was quite concerned.

20
00:01:29,899 --> 00:01:35,385
An-Najashi(النجاشي) is a religious person, and he doesn't want any heretics in his land.

21
00:01:36,228 --> 00:01:40,023
So, he recalled the Muslims again.

22
00:01:41,788 --> 00:01:46,950
Umm Salamah(ام سلمه) says there was nothing that worried us more than that event.

23
00:01:47,583 --> 00:01:49,281
It caused us great concern.

24
00:01:50,128 --> 00:01:53,580
Same thing we decided that we're going to speak the truth.

25
00:01:53,676 --> 00:01:55,438
 أن نَقُوْلَ الْحَقْ أينَ مَا كَانْ

26
00:01:55,871 --> 00:01:58,564
We're going to say what our Prophet has taught us.

27
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,171
We're gonna say the truth, no matter what happens.

28
00:02:03,204 --> 00:02:04,659
We're gonna speak the truth.

29
00:02:05,565 --> 00:02:08,472
Same thing Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جَعْفَر اِبْنِ اَبِيْ طَالِب) was to be their spokesman,

30
00:02:09,038 --> 00:02:13,854
and they went and An-Najashi(النجاشي) asked them, what do you say about Eesa(عيسى).?

31
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:17,650
He said; We say that he's the Messenger of Allah.

32
00:02:18,242 --> 00:02:20,250
Actually he first said that he's Abdullah(عبدالله).

33
00:02:21,352 --> 00:02:23,772
He said; He's a servant of Allah, he's a slave of Allah.

34
00:02:24,416 --> 00:02:25,995
He is the Messenger of Allah.

35
00:02:26,573 --> 00:02:32,391
He is the word of Allah, casted on Maryam(مريم),

36
00:02:32,612 --> 00:02:34,939
Mary, the chaste and virgin.

37
00:02:36,656 --> 00:02:37,866
The Negus said:

38
00:02:38,674 --> 00:02:43,180
There is no difference between what you say about him.

39
00:02:43,475 --> 00:02:46,453
And what we, or what I say about him,

40
00:02:46,692 --> 00:02:53,403
and immediately, the priests or the bishops started, he was hearing a commotion their sounds,

41
00:02:53,658 --> 00:02:56,653
they were angry, to hear this response from An-Najashi(النجاشي).

42
00:02:56,788 --> 00:02:58,118
How can he approve such a thing.?

43
00:02:59,153 --> 00:03:03,739
Even though it was all the same, with the exception of being the servant of Allah.

44
00:03:04,734 --> 00:03:08,456
But they said is the spirit of Allah that was blown into Maryam(مريم),

45
00:03:08,536 --> 00:03:12,325
the word of Allah that Mary was the chaste and virgin,

46
00:03:12,365 --> 00:03:17,922
it's all the same with except of this difference which is not a minor difference, it's a critical difference

47
00:03:18,471 --> 00:03:21,211
on whether Eesa(عيسى), Jesus is the son of Allah or not.

48
00:03:21,578 --> 00:03:30,283
Now, the Christians of Abyssinia would have been Orthodox Christians, who believed in the divinity of Jesus.

49
00:03:31,013 --> 00:03:34,476
 So, the priest didn't like, what they heard.

50
00:03:35,297 --> 00:03:41,450
An-Najashi(النجاشي) stood and said, say whatever you want to say, these people are going to be free in my land.

51
00:03:42,163 --> 00:03:46,822
Decisive decision was made that these people are going to get my protection.

52
00:03:48,339 --> 00:03:53,878
And Umm Salamah(ام سلمه) says that Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) and his partner were left with disgrace.

53
00:03:53,958 --> 00:03:57,823
because An-Najashi(النجاشي) drove them out and even gave them back their gifts.

54
00:04:00,238 --> 00:04:03,036
Because in the first visit of Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص).

55
00:04:03,433 --> 00:04:06,305
The first thing An-Najashi(النجاشي) asked Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) is,

56
00:04:06,415 --> 00:04:08,265
what did you bring me from your land.?

57
00:04:09,245 --> 00:04:12,013
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) said; I have brought you some leather products.

58
00:04:12,809 --> 00:04:17,442
And that was the best thing that An-Najashi(النجاشي) used to like, leather products.

59
00:04:18,076 --> 00:04:21,412
So, he had this friendship relationship between him and Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص).

60
00:04:22,665 --> 00:04:28,741
But when it came to principles, An-Najashi(النجاشي) stood with the truth,

61
00:04:29,286 --> 00:04:32,692
and he refused to hand over As-Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

62
00:04:34,079 --> 00:04:38,104
So that's the story of Al-Hijrah(الهجرة) to Abyssinia.

63
00:04:39,565 --> 00:04:42,264
Let's get on to some lessons,

64
00:04:43,012 --> 00:04:45,961
Number one, what were the reasons of this Hijrah(هجرة)?

65
00:04:47,504 --> 00:04:51,750
How come the Muslims fled their land and went to Abyssinia?

66
00:04:51,845 --> 00:04:59,181
How come they would leave the best place on the face of the earth Makkah and go somewhere else.?

67
00:05:00,511 --> 00:05:04,690
Well, the first reason is to flee persecution.

68
00:05:05,617 --> 00:05:08,374
They were being tortured in Makkah.

69
00:05:09,162 --> 00:05:13,307
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ allowed them to leave to flee from this persecution,

70
00:05:13,347 --> 00:05:17,500
so that they would free themselves from this physical pain.

71
00:05:17,788 --> 00:05:18,950
That's the first reason.

72
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:24,908
Ibn-Al-Hazm(ابن هزم), he says, when the number of Muslims increased and the persecution increased,

73
00:05:25,258 --> 00:05:26,810
Allah allowed them to migrate.

74
00:05:28,154 --> 00:05:31,421
Second reason, is to safeguard their faith.

75
00:05:33,132 --> 00:05:36,600
Not everyone will be able to handle the torture.

76
00:05:37,709 --> 00:05:39,844
Some people would give up their Eeman(ايمان).

77
00:05:40,690 --> 00:05:48,411
Not everyone has the strength of Bilal(بلال), not everyone can resist what Khabbab Ibn Arat(خباب إبن أرت) went through.

78
00:05:49,903 --> 00:05:53,841
So, if a person fears on the safety of their religion, they should go somewhere else.

79
00:05:55,087 --> 00:05:56,598
And Rasool Allah ﷺ says,

80
00:05:57,006 --> 00:05:58,688
لَا يُذلُّ الْمُؤمِنُ نَّفْسَه

81
00:05:59,073 --> 00:06:01,640
The believers should not humiliate themselves.

82
00:06:01,971 --> 00:06:04,578
يُعَرِّضُ نَفْسَه’ لِمَا لَا يُطِيْقُ مِنَّ الْبَلَاء

83
00:06:04,842 --> 00:06:08,226
By facing harm, which he is not able to handle.

84
00:06:09,378 --> 00:06:12,172
So, if it is too much for a person to handle

85
00:06:12,824 --> 00:06:15,620
then, they should not put themselves in that difficult situation.

86
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:19,117
To give you an example of what this concept means.

87
00:06:20,168 --> 00:06:26,938
There was once a man, who came to Rasool Allah ﷺ with a size of an egg, pure gold.

88
00:06:27,796 --> 00:06:33,210
And he gave it to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said, this is Sadaqah(صدقه), and it is all what I have.

89
00:06:34,857 --> 00:06:36,748
Rasool Allah ﷺ was upset and said:

90
00:06:37,191 --> 00:06:41,469
One of you would come and give up all of their wealth.

91
00:06:42,427 --> 00:06:45,699
And then after that, they would come and ask me for assistance.

92
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:53,440
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ did not want this person to give up all of his money and then ask for help.

93
00:06:53,916 --> 00:06:58,043
You keep your money, give what you're able to give, but keep some for yourself.

94
00:06:58,108 --> 00:06:59,860
Why do you come and say this all what I have.?

95
00:07:00,868 --> 00:07:06,721
But then we know that Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه at one point of time,

96
00:07:07,013 --> 00:07:11,320
 has given up all of his wealth to Rasool Allah ﷺ and Rasool Ullah praised that.

97
00:07:12,401 --> 00:07:15,204
How come the response of the Messenger of Allah was different.?

98
00:07:16,448 --> 00:07:21,371
Rasool Allah ﷺ knew in the situation of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), that he can handle the situation,

99
00:07:21,944 --> 00:07:27,282
he can give up all of his wealth and he would not get down to the level of begging.

100
00:07:28,595 --> 00:07:30,968
He will be able to take care of himself.

101
00:07:31,871 --> 00:07:35,045
However, not everyone is like Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

102
00:07:35,442 --> 00:07:41,507
So, for other people, they shouldn't put themselves in that difficult situation that they're not able to handle

103
00:07:41,531 --> 00:07:44,899
you give up everything in that moment of high emotions.

104
00:07:45,173 --> 00:07:50,142
But after that when things calm down, you start rethinking and saying; O, what have I done?

105
00:07:50,735 --> 00:07:52,905
I've given up all of my money, what can I do now.

106
00:07:54,749 --> 00:07:57,664
So, not everybody will be able to handle what is going on in Makkah

107
00:07:57,689 --> 00:08:00,826
therefore Rasool Allah ﷺ told them to leave and safeguard your religion.

108
00:08:01,589 --> 00:08:06,803
Ibn Is'haqq(اِبْنِ اِسْحَاقْ) says the Muslims then left towards Abyssinia fearing for their faith.

109
00:08:07,331 --> 00:08:12,708
Number three, we have a quote here by Syed Qutub(سيد قطب), he says,

110
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:18,022
 before I read this quote, and what is your impression of the people who went to Abyssinia.?

111
00:08:18,433 --> 00:08:21,675
Were they strong and noble among Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) or were they, the weak.?

112
00:08:23,399 --> 00:08:26,703
They belong to the strong and wealthy families of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

113
00:08:27,261 --> 00:08:29,017
and Syed Qutub(سيد قطب) states:

114
00:08:29,667 --> 00:08:35,819
It would not be correct to say that they had gone there for reasons of personal safety alone.

115
00:08:36,703 --> 00:08:44,320
For they included some of the most powerful and wealthiest of the prophet's followers and of his fellow tribesmen.

116
00:08:45,133 --> 00:08:48,847
The majority of them were from the tribe of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) including Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جَعْفَر اِبْنِ اَبِيْ طَالِب)

117
00:08:49,134 --> 00:08:55,477
and a number of young men who are accustomed to providing protection to the Prophet ﷺ such as Az-Zubair Bin Awaam(الزبير بن عوام),

118
00:08:55,794 --> 00:09:00,584
Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبد الرحمن ابن عوف), Abu Salamah Al-Makhzoomi(ابو سلمه المخزومي), Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) to mention a few.

119
00:09:01,626 --> 00:09:05,441
There were women belonging to some of the most prominent families of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

120
00:09:05,540 --> 00:09:08,669
such as Umm Habiba(ام حبيبه), daughter of Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان),

121
00:09:09,112 --> 00:09:12,268
the Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)'s unrivaled non Muslim leader,

122
00:09:12,608 --> 00:09:14,900
who would have never been persecuted in Makkah.

123
00:09:15,045 --> 00:09:19,333
Umm Habiba(ام حبيبه) would never have been persecuted in Makkah, no one would be able to touch her.

124
00:09:19,708 --> 00:09:22,940
She's the daughter of Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان), the leader of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

125
00:09:23,568 --> 00:09:28,126
There were no doubt other reasons for the Muslims immigration to Abyssinia,

126
00:09:28,682 --> 00:09:34,647
there was the need to shake the religious and social foundations of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)'s, most noble and powerful families,

127
00:09:35,355 --> 00:09:40,325
there could be no greater insult or threat to the Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) dynasties,

128
00:09:40,711 --> 00:09:47,408
that seeing their proudest and most noble sons and daughters running away for conscientious and religious reasons,

129
00:09:48,271 --> 00:09:52,146
leaving the cultural heritage and tribal homeland behind.

130
00:09:52,781 --> 00:09:59,279
So, the ones who made Hijrah(هجرة) belonging to the wealthy and strong families of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

131
00:09:59,828 --> 00:10:05,442
having them leave, according to the view of Syed Qutub(سيد قطب)

132
00:10:06,078 --> 00:10:10,280
is to cause an embarrassment and to shake the structure of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

133
00:10:11,242 --> 00:10:16,253
and Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)'s position in Arabia wasn't because of the strength of its army.

134
00:10:16,914 --> 00:10:21,239
Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were small in number, nevertheless, no one dare to attack them.

135
00:10:21,836 --> 00:10:28,751
And they used to be held in very high esteem, they had this deep respect in the hearts of everyone around them.

136
00:10:29,418 --> 00:10:31,960
And that was because of the values that they had.

137
00:10:32,343 --> 00:10:36,105
It was also because of their location next to the house of Allah

138
00:10:36,345 --> 00:10:39,733
and the fact that they are the guardians of Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

139
00:10:40,331 --> 00:10:49,880
So, for the people to see that the noblest, among their men and women had to leave Makkah,

140
00:10:50,552 --> 00:10:55,774
to flee for the safety of their religion was such an embarrassment for the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

141
00:10:56,152 --> 00:10:59,500
 and it would shake their foundations in Arabia.

142
00:11:00,736 --> 00:11:04,399
According to another author Munir Ghardaan(منير ألغردان).

143
00:11:04,763 --> 00:11:13,597
His view is that Rasool Allah ﷺ wanted to have a secondary base, outside of Makkah,

144
00:11:14,346 --> 00:11:18,942
so that if something happens in Makkah, at least the religion can survive somewhere else.

145
00:11:19,842 --> 00:11:26,421
And now since the number increased, the Muslims could spare dividing into two groups.

146
00:11:27,065 --> 00:11:31,201
One group stays in Makkah, one group would leave and stay in Abyssinia.

147
00:11:31,519 --> 00:11:37,961
And what will strengthen this view, is the fact that the Muslims in Abyssinia, never went back

148
00:11:39,213 --> 00:11:43,151
to meet the Prophet ﷺ when he was in Madina, until the seventh year of Hijrah(هجرة).

149
00:11:44,156 --> 00:11:49,707
They waited seven years after Rasool Allah ﷺ made Hijrah(هجرة) to travel back to Madina.

150
00:11:50,545 --> 00:11:55,082
And they weren't enjoying their stay, they wanted to be close Rasool Allah ﷺ,

151
00:11:55,399 --> 00:11:59,175
but they stayed there, until they got the permission from Rasool Allah ﷺ to come,

152
00:11:59,682 --> 00:12:04,895
and Rasool Allah ﷺ gave them this permission when it was safe for them to come back.

153
00:12:05,212 --> 00:12:07,373
Now Islam is firmly established.

154
00:12:07,611 --> 00:12:11,945
Because in the first few years in Madina, Madina was under constant threat.

155
00:12:13,294 --> 00:12:15,226
And the Muslims never really had safety.

156
00:12:15,950 --> 00:12:18,891
Just because they had the state didn't mean that they were secure.

157
00:12:19,129 --> 00:12:23,276
They were always under threat from an attack from one direction or another.

158
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:30,746
But after seven years, Islam was now had its roots deep, it was firmly established, it was strong.

159
00:12:31,118 --> 00:12:33,518
That's when the Sahabah came back from Abyssinia.

160
00:12:35,382 --> 00:12:37,522
Now, brothers and sisters,

161
00:12:37,987 --> 00:12:41,593
I'm spending more time than usual on this story of Al-Hijrah(الهجرة).

162
00:12:41,741 --> 00:12:45,875
Usually in books of Seerah(سيرة), there were just glance over the whole thing in few pages, and that's it.

163
00:12:46,828 --> 00:12:48,941
But we're spending a lot of time on this.

164
00:12:49,448 --> 00:12:53,626
We've already spend some time on the early session, and we'll spend some time this session

165
00:12:54,436 --> 00:12:59,301
because of the importance of Al-Hijrah(هجرة) to Al-Habasha(اَلْحَبَشَه) in our situation.

166
00:13:01,197 --> 00:13:04,934
This was a Muslim minority, living among Non-Muslim majority.

167
00:13:05,975 --> 00:13:08,793
It was a predominantly Christian country.

168
00:13:10,309 --> 00:13:12,677
So, there are some resemblances there.

169
00:13:13,153 --> 00:13:21,063
But when it comes to An-Najashi(النجاشي), we don't have any personality similar to him, in the West.

170
00:13:22,088 --> 00:13:25,673
A deeply religious leader with justice.

171
00:13:26,495 --> 00:13:29,205
We haven't had anything like that.

172
00:13:29,997 --> 00:13:38,885
Maybe at one moment of time, laws and constitutions of the West, were somewhat close to the personality of An-Najashi(النجاشي).

173
00:13:39,729 --> 00:13:42,349
But that has pretty much changed now.

174
00:13:43,426 --> 00:13:47,411
But I still think that this is an important subject and we need to talk about it.

175
00:13:48,004 --> 00:13:55,541
Now, unfortunately, there is not a lot of narrations that survived dealing with Al-Habasha(اَلْحَبَشَه) in particular,

176
00:13:55,598 --> 00:13:57,854
 and dealing with the Makkah era in general.

177
00:13:59,218 --> 00:14:03,564
If you open any book of Seerah(سيرة), you would find that for example, this book in front of me,

178
00:14:04,097 --> 00:14:14,974
as an example, the book is around 700 pages and the Makkah era is 150.

179
00:14:15,662 --> 00:14:24,963
So, hundred and fifty pages are dealing with 13 years of the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ and everything before that.

180
00:14:26,219 --> 00:14:33,270
And then you have almost 600 pages dealing with the last 10 years of the life of Rasool Ullah.

181
00:14:33,738 --> 00:14:35,615
So, you can see the disproportion here.

182
00:14:36,551 --> 00:14:37,657
There's a few reasons for that.

183
00:14:37,708 --> 00:14:43,768
Number one, the documentation of Hadith(حديث) was not allowed, until the Muslims were in Madina.

