225
00:18:13,931 --> 00:18:16,656
who took care of Rasool Allah ﷺ and breast fed him.

226
00:18:17,670 --> 00:18:19,976
She was from Al-Habasha(اَلْحَبَشَه).

227
00:18:20,567 --> 00:18:23,679
According to Sahih Muslim(صحيح مسلم), she was from Abyssinia.

228
00:18:24,368 --> 00:18:30,528
And Umm Aimen(ام ايمن) wasn't just Abyssinian but her culture her language was Abyssinian.

229
00:18:30,874 --> 00:18:35,433
In one narration it states that she presented Rasool Allah ﷺ with this food.

230
00:18:36,091 --> 00:18:38,760
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ said: What is this?

231
00:18:39,486 --> 00:18:45,674
She said, this is a dish that we make in Abyssinia and I wanted you to try it.

232
00:18:47,182 --> 00:18:52,131
So, she was even cooking some Abyssinian dishes in Arabia.

233
00:18:52,992 --> 00:18:56,886
Her accent, she couldn't get rid of her Abyssinian accent.

234
00:18:57,193 --> 00:19:00,746
For example, according to Ibn Sa'ad(اِبْنِ سَعْد), when she would say

235
00:19:00,792 --> 00:19:02,360
سَلَامُ اللهِ عَلَيْكُمْ

236
00:19:02,841 --> 00:19:05,149
She means peace of Allah be upon him she would say

237
00:19:05,282 --> 00:19:06,743
سَلَامِ اللهِ عَلَيْكُمْ

238
00:19:07,357 --> 00:19:09,277
which means no peace on you.

239
00:19:10,011 --> 00:19:12,832
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ would tell her just say Salam(سلام).

240
00:19:13,049 --> 00:19:14,633
