371
00:28:53,140 --> 00:29:00,697
It's very evident in the early Muslims history that the Muslim sister had a very important role to play.

372
00:29:01,998 --> 00:29:04,161
The first Muslim was a woman.

373
00:29:04,983 --> 00:29:06,877
The first Shaheed(شهيد) in Islam was a woman.

374
00:29:07,055 --> 00:29:09,055
The first martyr was Sumaiyah(سميعه)

375
00:29:10,075 --> 00:29:13,587
you can see the participation of Muslim women in Hijrah(هجرة) to Abyssinia,

376
00:29:13,871 --> 00:29:17,050
their participation in the Hijrah(هجرة) to Madina,

377
00:29:17,468 --> 00:29:21,048
their participation in Jihad(جهاد), their participation in Jama'at(جماعة)

378
00:29:21,408 --> 00:29:23,423
their participation in teaching and learning.

379
00:29:24,068 --> 00:29:30,512
So, some of the artificial barriers that we have erected now did not exist in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

380
00:29:31,268 --> 00:29:35,638
I mean, among us today, are people who are carrying it to the both extremes.

381
00:29:36,468 --> 00:29:43,543
One extreme is that men and women can mix and laugh and joke and without no barriers, Hijab(حجاب) is optional.

382
00:29:44,013 --> 00:29:51,500
And then on the other extreme, even the voice of women is not allowed to be spoken in public.

383
00:29:52,198 --> 00:29:54,781
We might assume, to just have them live in different planet.

384
00:29:55,576 --> 00:30:00,735
So, these are two extremes, but we need to find the middle road.

385
00:30:01,102 --> 00:30:06,782
And I want to give you an example to show you, the relationship that men and women had in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

386
00:30:06,875 --> 00:30:12,135
In this conversation is relevant to the emigration to Al-Habasha(اَلْحَبَشَه).

387
00:30:12,711 --> 00:30:17,940
When the Muslims came back to Madina, in the seventh year of Hijrah(إلهجره),

388
00:30:19,224 --> 00:30:27,177
the wife of Jafar Ibn Abi Talib(جَعْفَر اِبْنِ اَبِيْ طَالِب), Asmaa Bint Umais(اَسْمَاء بِنْتِ عُمَيْس), she went to visit Hafsah(حَفْصَه),

389
00:30:27,831 --> 00:30:31,782
the daughter of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب), who is the wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

390
00:30:32,017 --> 00:30:34,085
so Asmaa Bint Umais(اَسْمَاء بِنْتِ عُمَيْس) went to visit her.

391
00:30:35,297 --> 00:30:38,895
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) came to visit his daughter

392
00:30:39,841 --> 00:30:44,379
and he came in and saw this woman sitting in her room, he told her: Who is this woman?

393
00:30:45,300 --> 00:30:46,074
She said:

394
00:30:46,371 --> 00:30:48,171
هَذِه أسْماء بِنْتِ عميْسْ؟

395
00:30:48,639 --> 00:30:49,898
This is a Asmaa Bint Umais(اَسْمَاء بِنْتِ عُمَيْس).

396
00:30:49,984 --> 00:30:50,833
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said

397
00:30:50,873 --> 00:30:51,832
آلْحَبَشِيَّهْ؟

398
00:30:52,073 --> 00:30:53,610
Is this the Abyssinian woman.?

399
00:30:54,046 --> 00:30:59,253
Not that she is from Abyssinia, but he was referring to the fact that she has been an Abyssinia for so long.

400
00:31:00,096 --> 00:31:01,558
Is this the Abyssinian woman.

401
00:31:01,718 --> 00:31:02,667
آلْبَحْرِيَّهْ؟

402
00:31:02,783 --> 00:31:04,681
Is this woman who came from the sea,?

403
00:31:05,455 --> 00:31:08,777
Because they had to cross the sea to get into Madina.

404
00:31:09,740 --> 00:31:11,174
Hafsah(حفصه) said: Yes.

405
00:31:11,763 --> 00:31:13,977
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) told Asmaa(اَسْمَاء);

406
00:31:14,538 --> 00:31:17,076
we made Hijrah(هجرة) before you.

407
00:31:18,192 --> 00:31:21,881
Therefore we have more rights to Rasool Allah ﷺ then you do.

408
00:31:23,368 --> 00:31:26,337
Straight like that, he went to her and said: We made Hijrah(هجرة) before you.

409
00:31:26,590 --> 00:31:31,900
Therefore we are closer to Rasool Ullah than you and we have more rights to him than you do.

410
00:31:32,535 --> 00:31:36,761
Asmaa(اَسْمَاء) was quite angry by that statement, and she said:

411
00:31:37,010 --> 00:31:39,699
No, you're not closer to Rasool Allah ﷺ than us.

412
00:31:40,730 --> 00:31:43,131
You were with the Messenger of Allah.

413
00:31:43,517 --> 00:31:45,947
He was feeding the hungry among you,

414
00:31:45,971 --> 00:31:50,669
teaching the ignorant among you, while we were in a distant, despised land.

415
00:31:52,143 --> 00:31:55,634
We were in a faraway land and despised, we weren't very comfortable over there.

416
00:31:56,180 --> 00:32:00,031
We didn't like it being far away from Rasool Allah ﷺ.

417
00:32:00,701 --> 00:32:05,924
We were feeling homesick to the Messenger of Allah, not to Makkah, it was to the Messenger of Allah, we want to be with him.

418
00:32:07,186 --> 00:32:10,575
And then she said: I'm going to go and tell Rasool Allah ﷺ what you're saying now

419
00:32:10,615 --> 00:32:14,143
and I'm not gonna add anything to it, or subtract anything, I'm going to say it as you said it.

420
00:32:15,358 --> 00:32:18,769
And she went to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said: This is what Umar(عُمَر) told me.

421
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:21,678
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: And what did you say?

422
00:32:22,770 --> 00:32:25,580
She said: And she repeated the same statement,

423
00:32:25,828 --> 00:32:35,051
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: No, Umar(عُمَر) and his companions do not have more rights than you do, to me.

424
00:32:35,756 --> 00:32:38,463
They're not closer to me than you.

425
00:32:38,691 --> 00:32:45,043
They have the rewards of one Hijrah(هجرة) and you have the rewards of two Hijrah(هجرة).

426
00:32:46,021 --> 00:32:47,974
You get double the reward that they do.

427
00:32:48,572 --> 00:32:53,429
Asmaa Bint Umais(اَسْمَاء بِنْتِ عُمَيْس) said; When Rasool Allah mentioned this Hadith(حديث) to me,

428
00:32:54,160 --> 00:33:01,332
 the Sahabah who were in Abyssinia, Abu Musa Al-Asha'ari(ابو مُوسَى اَلْعَشْعَرِيْ) and his friends will come to me in large groups,

429
00:33:02,165 --> 00:33:05,676
all trying to learn this Hadith(حديث), of Rasool Allah ﷺ from me.

430
00:33:05,922 --> 00:33:10,186
And she said: There was nothing better for them in the world than this Hadith(حديث).

431
00:33:10,538 --> 00:33:14,940
This Hadith(حديث) was so valuable to them, it was worth the world and everything in it.

432
00:33:16,514 --> 00:33:18,325
So now, here you see that,

433
00:33:18,622 --> 00:33:26,029
first of all, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is speaking to this woman, and they're having a conversation.

434
00:33:26,748 --> 00:33:29,802
And it was a straightforward conversation.

435
00:33:30,538 --> 00:33:37,225
And then Asmaa Bint Umais(اَسْمَاء بِنْتِ عُمَيْس) is teaching the Sahabah, Abu Musa Al-Asha'ari(ابو مُوسَى اَلْاَشْعَرِيْ) and the other men about this Hadith(حديث).

436
00:33:37,741 --> 00:33:40,462
So, this was the nature of the relationship that existed.

437
00:33:40,990 --> 00:33:47,698
Obviously, if you look at all of the references, we have that deal with the relationship of men and women,

438
00:33:47,890 --> 00:33:51,315
you would find that there was a an element of formality in their dealings,

439
00:33:52,642 --> 00:33:55,488
you wouldn't find any incidents where they would joke and laugh with each other.

440
00:33:55,965 --> 00:34:05,396
So, they knew their limits, but in the same time, it wasn't that extreme, as we might see, amongst Muslims now.

441
00:34:07,256 --> 00:34:14,072
An example of the participation and the strength of the early Muslims would be Umm Habibah(اُمِّ حَبِيْبَه).

442
00:34:14,783 --> 00:34:21,862
Ya'ani(يعني) Umm Habibah رضي الله عنها, keep in mind the following factors and see how difficult it was on her.

443
00:34:22,435 --> 00:34:27,605
Number one, she's the daughter of the unrivaled leader of Makkah, Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان).

444
00:34:28,763 --> 00:34:37,293
So for her, to leave that comfortable life, wealth, nobility in her society

445
00:34:37,373 --> 00:34:42,122
and go and live as a foreigner and an alien land, is not easy.

446
00:34:42,185 --> 00:34:45,139
So number one, she was the daughter of Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان).

447
00:34:45,646 --> 00:34:47,986
Number two, she's living in a foreign land.

448
00:34:48,147 --> 00:34:57,508
Number three, which was disastrous, when her husband reached to Abyssinia, he apostated and became Christian.

449
00:34:58,608 --> 00:35:02,781
He was one of the Sahabah who made Hijrah(هجرة), when he got there, he changed his mind.

450
00:35:04,177 --> 00:35:10,010
Now Obaid-Ul-Allah Bin Jahash(عبيدالله بن جحش), he went to different stages in his life.

451
00:35:10,066 --> 00:35:18,092
I mean, he kept on flipping back and forth before Islam, changing his mind and going into different religions.

452
00:35:18,140 --> 00:35:19,573
 So, this was his personality.

453
00:35:19,833 --> 00:35:24,620
So, when he got there to Al-Habasha(اَلْحَبَشَه), he just changed from being a Muslim, into being a Christian,

454
00:35:25,072 --> 00:35:28,059
and the most influential person on woman is her husband.

455
00:35:28,807 --> 00:35:32,849
And it was very difficult for Umm Habibah(اُمِّ حَبِيْبَه) to deal with this situation.

456
00:35:33,289 --> 00:35:38,444
Her husband opostating and becoming Christian, obviously after that, they had to separate.

457
00:35:39,083 --> 00:35:48,563
Keep all of these factors in mind and see how strong she was, how steadfast she was, and how she was able to hold firm on her religion.

458
00:35:50,710 --> 00:35:52,881
What is the ruling on Hijrah(هجرة)?

459
00:35:54,226 --> 00:36:03,057
Migration is compulsory, if a Muslim individual is unable to establish his basic Islamic practices in the land,

460
00:36:03,104 --> 00:36:05,821
 such as prayer fasting, and the Azaan(آذان),

461
00:36:06,207 --> 00:36:12,332
if a Muslim is unable to establish the essential practices of Islam, then they must find somewhere else.

462
00:36:13,554 --> 00:36:19,907
It is permissible, if a Muslim is confronted with problems that make life difficult in that land,

463
00:36:20,281 --> 00:36:25,076
he is permitted to leave his land to another land of Islam seeking relief.

464
00:36:25,540 --> 00:36:33,202
Number three, it is forbidden if by leaving a Muslim neglects the Islamic duty in his land that no one can replace him in.

465
00:36:33,658 --> 00:36:40,205
If someone is playing a critical role, and nobody can step in and take that role, that is forbidden for a person to leave.

466
00:36:41,699 --> 00:36:44,763
What is the ruling on living among non Muslims.?

467
00:36:45,676 --> 00:36:50,838
And that is one topic that Muslims in the West have been avoiding talking about.

468
00:36:51,136 --> 00:36:55,343
We shy away from certain topics because they're controversial, we don't want to deal with them.

469
00:36:55,707 --> 00:37:02,648
But eventually we'll be faced with real problems that will force us to deal with these issues.

470
00:37:02,997 --> 00:37:06,872
And we need to have frank discussions on such matters.

471
00:37:07,348 --> 00:37:13,960
We can just throw them in the closet, brush them under the carpet and think that they will go away.

472
00:37:15,436 --> 00:37:23,194
When it comes to living in a non Muslim land, it is the consensus of Muslim scholars that it is not allowed.

473
00:37:24,624 --> 00:37:26,790
And the Ahadith(احاديث) are very clear.

474
00:37:27,754 --> 00:37:30,911
اَنَا بَرِيْءٌ مِمَّنْ اِقَامَةْ بَيْنَ ظَهْرَانِي الْمُشْرِكِيْنْ

475
00:37:31,171 --> 00:37:38,894
I have nothing to do with a Muslim, who lives among the ones, who associate God's besides Allah.

476
00:37:40,543 --> 00:37:45,211
This is one Hadith(حديث) of many, different narrations.

477
00:37:46,569 --> 00:37:48,811
The scholars gave exceptions.

478
00:37:49,026 --> 00:38:00,846
They said: If a person is propagating the message of Islam and is practicing Islam freely, then that is an excuse for them to stay.

479
00:38:02,005 --> 00:38:10,371
They also gave temporary excuse for somebody who's doing business or seeking knowledge.

480
00:38:11,398 --> 00:38:16,968
But this is on a temporary basis, it is not to settle indefinitely.

481
00:38:17,464 --> 00:38:23,527
Therefore, it is not allowed for us to live in non Muslim environments

482
00:38:23,671 --> 00:38:26,636
unless we are fulfilling our responsibilities of Da'wah(دعوة).

483
00:38:28,227 --> 00:38:33,664
Otherwise, we are accumulating sins by default.

484
00:38:35,051 --> 00:38:37,567
So, Da'wah(دعوة) is not an optional thing for us.

485
00:38:37,663 --> 00:38:44,249
But it is something that justifies a Muslim living in a Non-Muslim society.

486
00:38:44,824 --> 00:38:49,569
And by Da'wah(دعوة), we need to understand this in a comprehensive way.

487
00:38:50,404 --> 00:38:54,174
It doesn't mean that every single person needs to do the same thing.

488
00:38:54,955 --> 00:39:00,456
We mean Da'wah(دعوة) in a comprehensive way, anything that is serving the welfare of Islam,

489
00:39:00,870 --> 00:39:05,525
anything that serves the propagation of the message, would fall under Daw'ah(دعوة).

490
00:39:05,614 --> 00:39:10,625
It doesn't necessarily mean that you're distributing leaflets to non Muslims, or you're giving speeches to them.

491
00:39:11,083 --> 00:39:13,922
These are two ways but there are many others.

492
00:39:14,866 --> 00:39:19,445
Relief work is work of Da'wah(دعوة), charitable work is work of Da'wah(دعوة),

493
00:39:19,914 --> 00:39:22,613
teaching Muslims living in the West is a work of Da'wah(دعوة) too.

494
00:39:23,390 --> 00:39:27,610
So, we need to understand this concept of Da'wah(دعوة) in a comprehensive way.

495
00:39:30,818 --> 00:39:34,660
Uthman Ibn Madh'oon(عثمان إبن مظعون), was one of the Muhajireen(مهاجرين), who were in Abyssinia.

496
00:39:34,693 --> 00:39:39,198
He came back to Makkah and since he left he had to come in with some protection.

497
00:39:39,619 --> 00:39:46,667
So, he sought protection or he was offered protection by Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(الوليد بن مغيره), who was one of the elders of Makkah.

498
00:39:47,382 --> 00:39:58,540
Uthman Ibn Madh'oon(عثمان إبن مظعون), he entered into Makkah, he saw that every other Muslim is going through persecution except for himself.

499
00:39:59,225 --> 00:40:03,243
This didn't make him happy, he felt jealous.

500
00:40:04,153 --> 00:40:11,510
How come everyone else is going through this purification of their sins except myself.?

501
00:40:11,977 --> 00:40:17,263
So, he went to Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(الوليد بن مغيره) and told him I don't need your protection, I'm giving it, back to you.

502
00:40:17,659 --> 00:40:19,165
He said: Why my son, are you doing that?

503
00:40:19,243 --> 00:40:21,457
He said: I want the protection of Allah.

504
00:40:22,076 --> 00:40:23,442
I don't want your protection.

505
00:40:24,590 --> 00:40:30,416
He said, Well, since I have given you protection publicly, you have to give it back publicly.

506
00:40:30,488 --> 00:40:33,925
So, they went next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه) and Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(الوليد بن مغيره) said:

507
00:40:33,967 --> 00:40:37,225
Uthman Ibn Madh'oon(عثمان إبن مظعون) has given me back my protection,

508
00:40:37,557 --> 00:40:39,242
Uthman Ibn Madh'oon(عثمان إبن مظعون) said: Yes,

509
00:40:39,485 --> 00:40:44,495
I did find Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(الوليد بن مغيره) to be a very trustworthy and honest man.

510
00:40:44,653 --> 00:40:48,927
But I want to be under the protection of Allah and Allah alone.

511
00:40:49,809 --> 00:40:56,190
Later on, he was sitting in a gathering around one of the famous poets of Arabia, Lubaid(لُبَيْد),

512
00:40:56,815 --> 00:40:59,712
and Lubaid(لُبَيْد) was reciting some of his poetry.

513
00:41:00,341 --> 00:41:01,116
And he said:

514
00:41:01,268 --> 00:41:04,453
كُلُّ شَيْءٍخَلَ الله بَاطِلٌ

515
00:41:05,189 --> 00:41:09,310
He said: Everything save God is vanity.

516
00:41:09,980 --> 00:41:11,401
Everything is going to go away.

517
00:41:12,742 --> 00:41:15,940
Uthman(عثمان) said: Yes, you are right.

518
00:41:16,691 --> 00:41:18,829
This was a gathering that has held a lot of people.

519
00:41:19,295 --> 00:41:20,802
And then it continued and said:

520
00:41:21,224 --> 00:41:24,237
وَكُلُّ نَعِيْمٍ لَا مَحَالَةَ زَائِلٌ

521
00:41:24,872 --> 00:41:27,746
And all pleasures must fade.

522
00:41:28,242 --> 00:41:30,880
Uthman Ibn Madh'oon(عثمان إبن مظعون) interrupted and said: That's wrong.

523
00:41:31,764 --> 00:41:34,158
The pleasures of Paradise never fade away.

524
00:41:34,792 --> 00:41:39,623
Lubaid(لُبَيْد), being a respected, famous poet of Arabia was kind of shocked.

525
00:41:40,210 --> 00:41:44,376
How could someone in the audience respond to me like that?

526
00:41:45,337 --> 00:41:50,575
So he said; O, men, of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), those who sat with you used to not be so insulted.

527
00:41:50,855 --> 00:41:52,426
When did this come about so?

528
00:41:52,466 --> 00:41:54,507
When did this start happening among you?

529
00:41:55,137 --> 00:41:57,711
So one man, in the audience he said, don't worry about it.

530
00:41:57,751 --> 00:42:04,469
This is one of the fools who followed the religion of Muhammad(محمد), don't take it to heart.

531
00:42:05,417 --> 00:42:08,213
Uthman Ibn Madh'oon(عثمان إبن مظعون) responded and they had to fight.

532
00:42:08,462 --> 00:42:13,647
So, the man stood up and he punched Uthman Ibn Madh'oon(عثمان إبن مظعون) in his eye until the whole thing is black.

533
00:42:14,377 --> 00:42:17,280
Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(الوليد بن مغيره) saw this and he came to Uthman(عثمان) and said:

534
00:42:17,675 --> 00:42:20,961
there was no need for your eyes to go through that suffering.

535
00:42:22,677 --> 00:42:25,089
You were under my protection, why did you give it up?

536
00:42:26,099 --> 00:42:28,034
Uthman Ibn Madh'oon(عثمان إبن مظعون) said: No,

537
00:42:28,343 --> 00:42:36,228
he said; Not so, I swear, the only problem is that my good eye is in need of what the other one suffered for God's sake.

538
00:42:37,197 --> 00:42:44,267
Actually, I am under the protection of One stronger and more capable than yourself, O Ibn Abd-Sh-Shams(عبدالشمس).

539
00:42:44,966 --> 00:42:48,394
Al-Waleed(الوليد) offered again and said: Do you want to come back to my protection?

540
00:42:48,623 --> 00:42:51,165
He said: No, I want to be under the protection of Allah.

541
00:42:52,938 --> 00:42:56,208
And remember that some of these are Ahadith(احاديث), some of them are from Seerah(سيرة),

542
00:42:56,248 --> 00:42:59,858
we're trying to mix both to learn from Hadith(حديث) and to learn from Seerah(سيرة).

543
00:43:01,184 --> 00:43:07,383
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه, did not make Hijrah(هجرة) to Abyssinia, but he was suffering in Makkah.

544
00:43:07,463 --> 00:43:12,463
So, he requested permission from Rasool Allah ﷺ to allow him to migrate.

545
00:43:12,993 --> 00:43:14,495
Rasool Allah ﷺ gave him permission.

546
00:43:14,699 --> 00:43:19,017
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) left, he left Makkah and he reached to Yemen, Barkal Ghamad(برق الغماد),

547
00:43:19,097 --> 00:43:22,914
and then he met with Syed Al-Ahabeesh(سيد الأحابيش),

548
00:43:22,994 --> 00:43:26,397
Al-Ahabeesh(الأحابيش) are tribe that used to live close to Makkah.

549
00:43:26,888 --> 00:43:28,918
Ibn Dughanna(إبن دغنه), he met with him.

550
00:43:29,207 --> 00:43:32,358
Ibn Dughanna(إبن دغنه) told him, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) where are you heading towards?

551
00:43:32,891 --> 00:43:39,079
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: My people have offended me, treated me badly and forced me to leave.

552
00:43:40,057 --> 00:43:44,126
Ibn Dughanna(إبن دغنه) said: Such a person like you is an asset to his people.

553
00:43:44,953 --> 00:43:49,305
You are not a person to leave, and you are not the person to be driven out of your land.

554
00:43:49,934 --> 00:43:50,500
Why?

555
00:43:50,540 --> 00:43:55,912
He said: Because you aid those in distress and you are kindly towards the needy.

556
00:43:56,563 --> 00:43:59,349
And then he said: Go back, you are under my protection, and he took him to Makkah.

557
00:43:59,438 --> 00:44:01,202
And he went in front of the people of Makkah and said:

558
00:44:01,430 --> 00:44:02,751
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is under my protection.

559
00:44:02,888 --> 00:44:06,996
How can you drive out such a person from your land, he's an asset for you.

560
00:44:07,886 --> 00:44:09,504
You drive out to a person like Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

561
00:44:09,624 --> 00:44:10,898
He said: He's under my protection.

562
00:44:11,470 --> 00:44:14,969
The people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they came to Ibn Dughanna(إبن دغنه) and they said,

563
00:44:15,302 --> 00:44:17,578
Well, we accept your protection.

564
00:44:17,911 --> 00:44:22,446
But we are not going to allow Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to worship publicly.

565
00:44:23,474 --> 00:44:25,473
So, please make sure that he doesn't.

566
00:44:26,396 --> 00:44:31,918
Ibn Dughanna(إبن دغنه) came to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and said: Your people don't want you to offend them, so don't worship publicly.

567
00:44:32,492 --> 00:44:34,124
Previously, what Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) would do.?

568
00:44:34,739 --> 00:44:37,668
Is he would pray outside in front of the people.

569
00:44:38,772 --> 00:44:42,402
And Ayesha(عائشه) said: My father used to be a man with a very soft heart.

570
00:44:43,322 --> 00:44:46,496
And when he would recite the verses of Qur'an, he would cry.

571
00:44:47,159 --> 00:44:53,162
So you would have all of the kids and women and men attracted around Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) watching him.

572
00:44:53,385 --> 00:44:55,704
And this turned the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) crazy.

573
00:44:56,321 --> 00:45:01,907
And they felt that this will be a Fitnah(فِتْنَه) for their people, seeing this Khasho'o(خشوع) in Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

574
00:45:02,874 --> 00:45:05,829
So, Ibn Dughanna(إبن دغنه) told Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) to worship privately, Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) agreed.

575
00:45:06,348 --> 00:45:11,060
For a while Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was praying in the privacy of his home and then he had an idea.

576
00:45:11,892 --> 00:45:15,861
He decided to make a Musallah(مصلى) in the Fanna'a(فناء) of Baitah(بيته).

577
00:45:15,912 --> 00:45:17,895
 Fanna'a(فناء) is an open area of the house.

578
00:45:18,519 --> 00:45:22,101
Usually you would have in some styles of Islamic architecture,

579
00:45:22,181 --> 00:45:27,672
you would have the house built in a square and in the middle it is empty.

580
00:45:28,642 --> 00:45:29,890
So, that would be Fanna'a(فناء).

581
00:45:30,789 --> 00:45:34,345
Or Fanna'a(فناء) could mean like a backyard or something a place that is open.

582
00:45:34,903 --> 00:45:36,077
But it's part of the house.

583
00:45:36,839 --> 00:45:39,703
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) took his Fanna'a(فناء) to be a Musallah(مصلى).

584
00:45:40,544 --> 00:45:44,782
So, even though it was inside his house, but people could see it from outside.

585
00:45:45,638 --> 00:45:47,746
So now, the same problem happened again,

586
00:45:47,802 --> 00:45:51,646
all of the people would gather until, it would be crowds outside the house of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), watching him pray.

587
00:45:52,370 --> 00:45:57,175
They were amazed by the Khusho'o(خشوع) that Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكر الصديق) had.

588
00:45:57,818 --> 00:46:01,516
And the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were furious, they went to Ibn Dughanna(إبن دغنه) and they said:

589
00:46:01,871 --> 00:46:04,638
We told you we don't want him to worship publicly.

590
00:46:05,153 --> 00:46:07,515
So, Ibn Dughanna(إبن دغنه) went to Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and spoke to him about it.

591
00:46:07,639 --> 00:46:10,340
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) said: I'll give your protection back, I don't need it.

592
00:46:10,955 --> 00:46:12,338
I'll be in the protection of Allah.

593
00:46:13,223 --> 00:46:16,855
And he did give up the protection of Ibn Dughanna(إبن دغنه).

594
00:46:17,184 --> 00:46:19,067
Few notes on the story of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

595
00:46:19,317 --> 00:46:20,279
Number one,

596
00:46:20,510 --> 00:46:23,567
when he met with Ibn Dughanna(إبن دغنه) and Ibn Dughanna(إبن دغنه), asked him:

597
00:46:24,049 --> 00:46:27,496
How come you are migrating from your land.?

598
00:46:28,056 --> 00:46:30,680
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) said, in one narration.

599
00:46:31,077 --> 00:46:35,681
اَسِيْحُ فِيْ الْاَرضْ وَ اَعْبُدُ رَبِّيْ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ اَعْبُدْ رَبِّيْ

600
00:46:36,067 --> 00:46:37,648
Why are you traveling? He said:

601
00:46:38,286 --> 00:46:39,026
Where are you going?

602
00:46:39,106 --> 00:46:43,722
He said: I want to travel in the land, in order to worship My Lord.

603
00:46:44,803 --> 00:46:48,299
So, now Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) is leaving with no purpose but to worship Allah

604
00:46:48,787 --> 00:46:52,825
to go in the land and worship Allah سبحانه وتعالى, seeking freedom.

605
00:46:53,256 --> 00:46:55,706
What will they do with that freedom? Worship Allah,

606
00:46:56,533 --> 00:47:02,217
they would use every resource that they have to please Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

607
00:47:03,320 --> 00:47:04,851
He wasn't traveling to do business.

608
00:47:04,915 --> 00:47:07,014
He was traveling, he said, I want to worship Allah.

609
00:47:07,424 --> 00:47:08,388
That's why I'm leaving.

610
00:47:09,603 --> 00:47:13,506
Second lesson, what did Ibn Dughanna(إبن دغنه) know about Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).?

611
00:47:14,259 --> 00:47:17,648
What was the reputation that Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) had, among the non Muslims?

612
00:47:18,328 --> 00:47:19,550
Caring for the needy,

613
00:47:20,166 --> 00:47:23,278
providing for the poor, sponsoring the orphan,

614
00:47:23,766 --> 00:47:25,407
standing up for right.

615
00:47:26,303 --> 00:47:28,242
That was the reputation of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر).

616
00:47:29,413 --> 00:47:34,051
He wasn't known for ill manners and corrupt character.

617
00:47:34,563 --> 00:47:36,960
He was known for these righteous values,

618
00:47:37,029 --> 00:47:43,365
which every person on the face of the earth, who has decency would recognize their value.

619
00:47:44,240 --> 00:47:47,286
And this should be the personality of the Muslim wherever they are.

620
00:47:47,797 --> 00:47:49,885
This is what the people know of you.

621
00:47:50,491 --> 00:47:57,599
 Your righteousness, your standing up for what is right, your charitable work.

622
00:47:58,294 --> 00:48:02,380
And that is what led Ibn Dughanna(إبن دغنه) to say that I'm going to give you protection,

623
00:48:02,444 --> 00:48:05,311
he said you are an asset for your people, we can't let you leave,

624
00:48:05,440 --> 00:48:06,917
we can't allow you to leave Makkah,

625
00:48:07,563 --> 00:48:11,432
your are a credit for them, you are pride for your people.

626
00:48:12,644 --> 00:48:15,064
And this should be the reputation of every Muslim.

627
00:48:15,279 --> 00:48:17,645
This is what the people should know about us.

628
00:48:19,509 --> 00:48:20,733
Number three,

629
00:48:21,411 --> 00:48:26,699
his Salah(صلاة) was his Da'wah(دعوة), publicly practicing the rituals of Islam is Da'wah(دعوة).

630
00:48:27,935 --> 00:48:29,660
For the people to see Hajj(حَجْ),

631
00:48:30,408 --> 00:48:32,986
for them to see our Aftaar(إفطار) in Ramadan(رمضان).

632
00:48:33,247 --> 00:48:39,905
We used to hold in our mosque, open dinners in Ramadan(رمضان), we would invite the neighborhood to come and break fasting with us.

633
00:48:40,195 --> 00:48:44,371
And some of them would even fast, they are non Muslims, they would fast, they would join in.

634
00:48:45,056 --> 00:48:49,094
In fact, many people seems to be enthusiastic to participate with Muslims in Ramadan(رمضان),

635
00:48:49,457 --> 00:48:51,120
let them do that, let them go ahead.

636
00:48:51,516 --> 00:48:57,221
Let them taste the value of Sayyam(صيام), the flavor of it, and invite them to have Iftaar(إفطار).

637
00:48:57,607 --> 00:49:01,412
Let them see the socialization that the Muslims have in Ramadan(رمضان).

638
00:49:02,010 --> 00:49:09,845
Salah(صلاة), Salat-Ut-Taraweh(صلاة التراويح), we shouldn't hide in our enclaves in our Masajid(مساجد) and close it off to the public.

639
00:49:09,885 --> 00:49:10,960
 This is Da'wah(دعوة).

640
00:49:11,578 --> 00:49:13,593
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) would do it in public.

641
00:49:13,775 --> 00:49:20,358
And the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) were furious, because they thought that this will attract the people to Islam,

642
00:49:20,980 --> 00:49:25,677
seeing Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), seeing the Khusho'o(خشوع) that he had will bring them closer to Allah سبحانه وتعالى.

643
00:49:26,389 --> 00:49:32,029
So, we should publicly do these Ibadaat(عبادات), because there is a special flavor in them.

644
00:49:32,370 --> 00:49:37,659
And there's a uniqueness in the rituals that Allah سبحانه وتعالى has prescribed on us.

645
00:49:39,456 --> 00:49:44,450
And that will also relate to number four, we should publicize the message,

646
00:49:44,841 --> 00:49:52,978
the enemies of Islam wouldn't mind if you're praying in your cubicle, that's your private life, we're not going to interfere with it,

647
00:49:53,361 --> 00:49:56,682
but they're going to be resistant to you doing it in public.

648
00:49:57,753 --> 00:49:59,311
And that is what we should do.

649
00:50:00,298 --> 00:50:05,843
Because we want to attract the good among all people to become Muslim.

650
00:50:06,798 --> 00:50:10,121
And the good heart will be attracted by good things.

651
00:50:11,614 --> 00:50:14,579
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرًا

652
00:50:14,621 --> 00:50:16,722
We finished Al-Hijrah(هجرة) ila'a(الى) Habasha(حَبَشَه).

